    <string name="onb1_title">Files — only with your permission</string>
    <string name="onb1_text">GitGo does not ask for access to all of your phone storage. You choose files and folders yourself in the system picker — the app sees only what you select and copies it into the repository working folder.</string>
    <string name="onb2_title">Fast sending</string>
    <string name="onb2_text">Many files and folders at once: parallel upload through the GitHub API in a single commit. The notification shows how much was sent, the speed and the time left.</string>
    <string name="onb3_title">Terminal and Git</string>
    <string name="onb3_text">A separate window with git commands: status, add, commit, push, pull, clone, branch, merge, stash and more. Notifications let you follow transfers in the background.</string>
